From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: pwrctrl: apple-wifi: Match the BCM4345

The iPod touch 6 (N102) has a BCM4345 Wi-Fi module on PCIe (14e4:43ab)
that powers up like the A8/A8X BCM4350: assert VDD (REG_ON on the PMIC
GPIO), wait 100 ms, and hold DEVICE_WAKE asserted while active.

Map pci14e4,43ab to the BCM4350 power-control sequence so the endpoint
node binds pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c
index cf90165..e8b4310 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c
@@ -226,6 +226,10 @@ static const struct of_device_id apple_wifi_pwrctrl_of_match[] = {
 		.compatible = "pci14e4,43a3",
 		.data = &apple_bcm4350_wifi_data,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible = "pci14e4,43ab",
+		.data = &apple_bcm4350_wifi_data,
+	},
 	{
 		.compatible = "pci14e4,43dc",
 		.data = &apple_j172_wifi_data,
